}}

==Enemy==
Cat God is no longer [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]]! He has a standing range of 300, but his attacks go up to 1,000. His attacks are now mixed; he will first cast God Bless You twice, which will [[Knockback]] AND [[Slow]] all cats within his reach with relatively low damage. He then prepares his lightning strike, which deals 65,999 damage at 100% strength magnification. Due to his initial buff being 1,100%, if the player does not have the [[Mystery Mask]] treasure, this enemy has a whopping '''16,499,989 HP''' and deals up to '''747,967 damage'''!

Like all the other Cat Gods, it's a requirement that the Mystery Mask is up to 100% to fully reduce his power.

==Strategy==
:''See [[The Big Bang (Cats of the Cosmos)]]''

In order to reduce his pushing power, cats with [[Knockback]] and [[Immune to Slow|Slow Immunity]] are recommended, Cats with [[Survive]] ability can endure his 3rd hit and prevent him from moving forward. [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|Anti-Traitless Cats]] can significantly help during the boss fight. [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Vendor Cat and Kitten]] shines against him. Knockback and [[Freeze]] resets his attack animation, while Knockback and Slow immunity prevent Cat God from pushing them back. Watch out for alien peons, though.

Rushers also benefit significantly from Cat God's first two attacks, as the knockback will reset their backswing, and the spacing between the two hits may allow them to land one additional hit. Given the right strategy, they can practically interrupt Cat God's attacks several times, eventually killing him if not removing large sections of his health. A prime example is [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], who can usually get at least 2-3 hits in, and with most of his damage concentrated into his first hit, he can remove ~200k in ideal circumstances, and even more if supported well.

